cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "clepsydra: Bayesian lexical dating from cognate lists"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tresoldi
    given-names: Tiago
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2863-1467"
    affiliation: "Department of Linguistics and Philology, Uppsala University"
url: "https://github.com/tresoldi/clepsydra"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tresoldi/clepsydra"
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
abstract: >-
  A C99 engine for dating language divergences from cognate data. It reports
  posterior distributions of lexical, relative and calendar node ages on a
  fixed tree or a sample of trees, with calibrations, dated tips, observation
  error, among-concept rate variation, strict and relaxed clocks, adequacy
  checks and model averaging by PSIS-LOO stacking.
keywords:
  - historical linguistics
  - lexical dating
  - glottochronology
  - phylogenetics
  - Bayesian inference
  - MCMC
  - cognates
